218
00:16:55,573 --> 00:17:01,458
Type it by hand in the lab shell. Your
commit IDs will differ from the transcript

219
00:17:01,498 --> 00:17:03,945
where you create commits yourself.

220
00:17:04,285 --> 00:17:06,808
Before you start, write
down three predictions:

221
00:17:07,148 --> 00:17:11,856
After git merge --abort, which of your
uncommitted edits are still there: the one

222
00:17:11,896 --> 00:17:16,779
you never staged, the one you staged before
the merge, the one you staged during it?

223
00:17:17,119 --> 00:17:20,264
What will git reflog -1
show after the abort?

224
00:17:20,604 --> 00:17:23,059
If an edit is lost, where could a copy of
it still exist, and which command would

225
00:17:23,099 --> 00:17:23,305
list it?

226
00:17:23,645 --> 00:17:27,304
The lab reproduces the loss from
the hook and recovers the edit.

227
00:17:27,344 --> 00:17:30,540
That's the lost prompt edit
from the start, found again.

228
00:17:30,580 --> 00:17:33,257
